WEBVTT

01:17.200 --> 01:18.330
Mom.

01:19.810 --> 01:20.590
Sora!

01:30.540 --> 01:31.480
Welcome back.

01:32.420 --> 01:33.580
I'm home.

01:37.000 --> 01:39.840
Sora-chan, you seem to be different than before.

01:39.840 --> 01:40.470
Huh?

01:40.470 --> 01:41.670
What do you mean by that?

01:41.670 --> 01:44.620
You have that "city dweller" look about you.

01:45.020 --> 01:45.850
Oh, really?

01:45.850 --> 01:47.280
Let's see.

01:46.530 --> 01:48.560
Hey, Mom!

01:48.950 --> 01:50.600
You're tickling me!

01:53.500 --> 01:57.820
I've really returned home, haven't I?

01:59.350 --> 02:00.900
Yeah, you sure have.

02:00.900 --> 02:04.200
It's fine, this is your hometown.

02:05.580 --> 02:10.200
You know, I have done a lot of "trial and error."

02:10.200 --> 02:11.580
Oh my.

02:11.580 --> 02:14.670
You can't keep making a lot of mistakes.

02:14.670 --> 02:15.680
That's right.

02:16.240 --> 02:17.170
I see.

02:27.180 --> 02:30.380
Chao, I'm back!

02:32.000 --> 02:33.310
Chao!

02:34.130 --> 02:36.650
Ah, it's Chao!

02:37.460 --> 02:38.610
Sora!

02:38.610 --> 02:40.820
Lunch is ready!

02:40.820 --> 02:42.060
Okay!

02:45.190 --> 02:48.620
Hara-sensei, during meal times, would always say the strangest things.

02:48.620 --> 02:50.160
It was really funny.

02:50.670 --> 02:51.790
Is that so?

02:51.790 --> 02:53.830
It's great that you had such a good teacher.

02:57.390 --> 03:00.840
He would suddenly exclaim, "Genghis Khan!"

03:00.840 --> 03:02.170
Really now?

03:09.740 --> 03:12.500
Ah, so delicious!

03:13.330 --> 03:14.680
This milk...

03:14.680 --> 03:16.940
Michiru-chan brought it over.

03:16.940 --> 03:18.730
It's milk from Yoshiko-baachan's place.

03:20.840 --> 03:23.080
I want Gouta-kun to drink it too.

03:23.810 --> 03:27.040
Sora, you met many people in Tokyo, didn't you?

03:27.310 --> 03:27.980
Yes.

03:28.590 --> 03:31.520
I'm glad I got to go to Tokyo.

04:05.930 --> 04:06.860
Father.

04:07.700 --> 04:10.450
I've also become a mage.

04:12.550 --> 04:15.100
I've made a lot of friends in Tokyo.

04:15.700 --> 04:17.530
I've also found someone I like.

04:19.120 --> 04:23.870
You know, being in love is painful, isn't it?

04:24.430 --> 04:25.840
My heart keeps beating rapidly.

04:27.040 --> 04:29.320
But it's so warm.

04:50.490 --> 04:51.280
Gouta.

05:22.010 --> 05:22.730
Sora.

05:49.460 --> 05:51.080
This is father's magic request.

05:55.670 --> 05:59.920
I worked hard for the sake of using this magic.

06:06.570 --> 06:08.360
Daddy!

06:11.590 --> 06:13.820
I've finished the flower necklace.

06:13.820 --> 06:15.980
I see, that was fast.

06:17.990 --> 06:19.470
What's the next request?

06:19.730 --> 06:22.800
Let's see, what should I ask for?

06:26.130 --> 06:27.310
This is amazing.

06:28.150 --> 06:30.670
Giving me a really hard one is fine too!

06:30.670 --> 06:36.140
Let's see... maybe Dad should write down what the best thing to see would be.

06:37.540 --> 06:39.860
The best...

06:42.070 --> 06:42.970
The best...

06:42.970 --> 06:44.060
The best...

06:44.220 --> 06:45.180
The best...

06:45.180 --> 06:46.230
The best...

06:46.230 --> 06:46.960
Sora!

06:47.770 --> 06:48.690
Okay!

06:53.490 --> 06:54.780
If you will, please.

06:54.780 --> 06:56.080
Yes, certainly!

07:06.250 --> 07:07.080
Sora...

07:08.570 --> 07:10.500
This will be my first job here.

07:14.440 --> 07:15.910
Warm memories.

07:17.050 --> 07:18.720
Recalling memories.

07:19.900 --> 07:22.870
Now, for the sake of the person I love...

07:30.360 --> 07:31.730
putting my heart into it...

07:35.910 --> 07:38.000
Father... Mother...

07:38.580 --> 07:41.280
Thank you for taking care of me for so long.

07:42.180 --> 07:44.140
Sora, you're very beautiful.

07:45.050 --> 07:48.490
Definitely, a very beautiful bride.

07:51.650 --> 07:56.620
I'm really happy to be your daughter.

09:06.520 --> 09:07.280
Yes.

09:08.480 --> 09:11.340
The Magic Bureau will contact you later.

09:12.190 --> 09:12.960
Yes.

09:14.300 --> 09:15.290
Thanks for your help.

09:17.210 --> 09:18.750
Which child is it this time?

09:19.400 --> 09:21.370
A brat from Osaka.

09:22.210 --> 09:26.170
Then does this mean you're taking that five-year project?

09:26.730 --> 09:29.430
It's nothing compared to your work, Sayori-chan.

09:29.430 --> 09:31.220
Don't you mean Sayori-obaasan?

09:31.220 --> 09:32.120
Yes, yes.

09:33.740 --> 09:35.180
Good morning!

09:35.540 --> 09:36.400
Yo!

09:36.400 --> 09:39.420
The new trainee is coming today, right?

09:39.700 --> 09:40.390
Yes.

09:41.140 --> 09:42.590
I hope that we all get along.

09:50.250 --> 09:53.960
It's pointless for me to be a mage.

09:54.500 --> 09:56.460
Okay, what is it this time?

09:58.000 --> 10:01.860
Because... people with sad faces...

10:04.540 --> 10:08.470
There are many times when magic won't work.

10:08.470 --> 10:09.390
What?

10:09.390 --> 10:10.680
Even for you, senpai?

10:11.350 --> 10:15.240
Yes, the most important thing is to not repeat your mistakes.

10:15.970 --> 10:16.710
Okay.

10:18.790 --> 10:22.550
There's a friend of mine who can use magic really well.

10:23.030 --> 10:25.380
Better than you, senpai?

10:26.160 --> 10:26.890
Yes.

10:27.520 --> 10:31.270
I realized that after I had met that person,

10:32.690 --> 10:34.840
magic isn't about skills.

10:37.560 --> 10:39.460
The most important thing is...

10:40.240 --> 10:43.630
to take your client's feelings into you...

10:43.630 --> 10:46.930
so that you truly feel what your clients feel.

10:47.700 --> 10:50.680
The feeling of the people...

10:53.160 --> 10:55.940
Your tears, Kurihara, are tears of kindness.

10:56.780 --> 11:00.370
That's why I think you are suited to become a mage.

11:00.940 --> 11:01.660
Yes!

11:02.060 --> 11:04.200
I'll give it my best!

11:10.160 --> 11:14.370
Senpai, I found a place with delicious drinks!

11:14.370 --> 11:16.280
Oh?  That's great!

11:19.310 --> 11:20.340
What?

11:20.780 --> 11:22.500
We're reserving the tickets?

11:23.030 --> 11:24.300
Yes.

11:24.670 --> 11:26.880
Because the job hunt is over.

11:26.880 --> 11:29.300
Let's get the tickets and go.

11:29.300 --> 11:32.930
But at this time in Biei, there aren't any places to stay.

11:33.420 --> 11:35.070
That's just common opinion.

11:36.310 --> 11:40.430
We should just go and look for people who've cancelled.

11:41.480 --> 11:43.890
I see, as expected of Asagi.

11:44.690 --> 11:47.190
But if we stay over at Suzuki's place...

11:47.190 --> 11:47.840
We can't.

11:49.890 --> 11:52.050
It can't be Suzuki Sora's place.

11:57.190 --> 11:58.090
That's right...

11:59.140 --> 11:59.830
Because...

11:59.830 --> 12:01.040
When we're in Biei...

12:02.380 --> 12:03.730
let's go eat ice cream.

12:07.950 --> 12:12.580
Sora said to try the roadside station's ice cream because it's really delicious.

12:13.700 --> 12:14.720
Suzuki-san...

12:15.560 --> 12:17.250
I wonder where she's working.

12:20.390 --> 12:21.860
Suzuki Sora...

12:22.960 --> 12:25.530
she really is a great mage.

12:51.750 --> 12:53.840
Hello, I'm Yasuko.

12:53.840 --> 12:55.840
Hello!

12:56.210 --> 12:59.330
Thanks to everyone who came out today.

12:59.680 --> 13:01.140
I'm really happy.

13:01.140 --> 13:02.220
Yasuko!

13:02.220 --> 13:03.600
Yasuko-san!

13:03.600 --> 13:05.050
Yasu-chan!

13:07.190 --> 13:10.360
So then, I wonder what I should sing next...

13:10.360 --> 13:12.230
I want to hear the "Jellyfish" song!

13:12.230 --> 13:14.240
How about a Rooster's cover?

13:14.510 --> 13:19.510
I often sing by myself on the road,

13:20.650 --> 13:22.540
although I haven't gone there in a while.

13:22.540 --> 13:23.580
We know.

13:23.580 --> 13:24.750
We've heard.

13:24.870 --> 13:25.660
Me too.

13:25.750 --> 13:26.410
Me too.

13:28.480 --> 13:29.350
Thank you.

13:30.130 --> 13:31.380
Perhaps I should go again.

13:32.040 --> 13:32.770
But you know...

13:33.430 --> 13:35.570
during that time, I made up a song.

13:36.160 --> 13:37.200
Please listen to it.

13:38.760 --> 13:40.140
"Shimokitazawa."

16:20.600 --> 16:22.310
What's the matter, young man?

16:23.670 --> 16:24.510
Sorry.

16:25.190 --> 16:27.120
Could you give me some directions?

16:27.650 --> 16:28.970
Are you from the mainland?

16:29.240 --> 16:29.930
Yes.

16:30.600 --> 16:31.840
I'm from Kanagawa.

16:32.130 --> 16:33.900
What do you think of Hokkaido?

16:35.800 --> 16:39.540
The sky is large; it has a very good feeling.

16:39.930 --> 16:41.480
I like it.

16:42.100 --> 16:43.110
Thanks.

16:43.500 --> 16:47.640
Um... about this wide place with only one tree...

16:48.600 --> 16:50.380
I wonder if it's that place...

16:56.790 --> 16:57.750
Yes, it is.

16:58.000 --> 17:00.340
Okay, continue down this road.

17:00.340 --> 17:02.930
Then make a turn there and you'll see it.

17:05.900 --> 17:07.080
Thank you very much.

17:08.120 --> 17:11.120
Young man, why are you in Hokkaido?

17:12.110 --> 17:13.220
To meet someone.

17:13.900 --> 17:14.640
My girlfriend.

17:15.080 --> 17:17.370
Oh, isn't it great to be young!

17:18.430 --> 17:19.180
Later.

17:21.360 --> 17:22.170
Young man!

17:29.030 --> 17:31.540
Our tomatoes are really delicious.

17:33.150 --> 17:33.980
Thank you!

17:55.530 --> 17:56.280
Sora.

17:57.440 --> 17:58.720
I've finally met you.

18:07.230 --> 18:08.340
It's this scenery.

18:10.710 --> 18:12.870
Sora, have you been lonely?

18:16.420 --> 18:17.510
I've been alright...

18:21.850 --> 18:23.640
because I've always been with you, Sora.

18:41.860 --> 18:44.400
Gouta-kun doesn't like tomatoes.

18:45.190 --> 18:47.650
I've hated them ever since I was young.

18:47.650 --> 18:50.370
Hokkaido's tomatoes are really tasty.

18:50.800 --> 18:51.730
Hmm?

18:52.170 --> 18:55.080
At home, I would also make tomato juice.

18:55.830 --> 18:58.060
I want Gouta-kun to try it.

18:58.750 --> 19:00.040
Is it really that delicious?

19:00.040 --> 19:02.530
Yes, it's the best in the world!

19:03.730 --> 19:05.380
Make it for me next time, then.

19:05.380 --> 19:06.910
Then come to Biei.

19:14.130 --> 19:16.650
Sora, it really IS delicious!

19:16.960 --> 19:17.690
Sora!

19:24.720 --> 19:25.770
Maldives.

19:25.770 --> 19:26.940
Sri Lanka.

19:26.940 --> 19:28.020
Lombok.

19:28.020 --> 19:29.040
Montebello.

19:29.350 --> 19:30.050
Fiji.

19:30.450 --> 19:31.190
Samoa.

19:31.620 --> 19:32.530
Tahiti.

19:32.530 --> 19:33.310
Hawaii.

19:34.390 --> 19:35.720
Caroline Islands.

19:37.110 --> 19:38.760
I got to see the world's oceans.

19:39.810 --> 19:41.570
The world really is amazing.

19:42.070 --> 19:44.030
I am no longer an amateur surfer.

19:46.770 --> 19:47.530
Sora.

19:48.490 --> 19:51.000
I don't know when I'll be able to meet you again.

19:52.130 --> 19:53.520
I'm doing my best in the world...

19:54.150 --> 19:56.510
and I'll re-tell it all to you.

19:58.550 --> 20:01.090
Well then, I have to get going.

20:05.990 --> 20:06.700
Okay.

20:07.730 --> 20:11.500
Sora, I'll show you all the oceans I've seen.

20:14.620 --> 20:16.400
The oceans within my memories...

20:17.960 --> 20:18.680
right here...

20:19.970 --> 20:21.370
for the one I love.

20:25.830 --> 20:27.030
Putting my heart into it...

20:51.650 --> 20:53.030
Putting my heart into it...
